22|f|laser observations span only 0.25 m of range (10 observations; gate 0.6 m). The lever arm, not the count, fixes the fitted direction: at this spread one pixel of dot-label noise moves every length by several percent. Shoot the target at two clearly different distances. Refusing to persist. The refusal is recorded, so this dive has left the calibration cohort and nothing is retrying it. It returns on its own once any laser or slate label on it is newer than the refusal, so relabelling is enough and there is no flag to clear. If its observations cannot be fixed, park it with Priority.NONE and a note; for a checkerboard dive that needs different frames rather than better labels, clear its calibration target via DELETE /api/v1/dives/{id}/calibration-target/.|10|
