103|f|fitted laser baseline 6.25 cm is outside the plausible range 7.8-14.5 cm. The baseline is a property of the camera+laser rig, not of the dive, and the fleet sits at ~10.4 cm; a value this far off means the fit, not the hardware. It would scale every depth and every length by that factor, invisibly to reprojection residual and to the self-consistency gate. Refusing to persist. This dive stays in the calibration cohort and will be re-selected hourly, blocking higher-id dives: either fix its observations, or park it with Priority.NONE and a note, or (checkerboard dives) clear its calibration target via DELETE /api/v1/dives/{id}/calibration-target/.|17|
